<section class="chapter" aria-label="What signals are">
  <div class="chapter__inner">
    <h2 class="section-title">What signals are</h2>

    <p class="muted">
      A signal is a <strong>comparable input captured consistently across workflows</strong>.
      Signals allow the system to detect patterns, measure performance, and identify bottlenecks
      without relying on interpretation or memory.
    </p>

    <p>
      Signals are not dashboards and they are not opinions.
      They are the structured inputs that make measurement possible.
    </p>

    <div class="miniGrid miniGrid--4">
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Comparable</b>
        <span>Signals must mean the same thing across teams and tools.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="mini">
        <b>Observable</b>
        <span>Signals are derived from real events or structured inputs.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="mini">
        <b>Traceable</b>
        <span>Every signal can be tied to a workflow event or input.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="mini">
        <b>Actionable</b>
        <span>Signals exist to support decisions, not reporting vanity.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      Without shared signals, organizations end up arguing about numbers instead of fixing the system.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" aria-label="Signals vs metrics">
  <div class="chapter__inner">
    <h2 class="section-title">Signals vs Metrics</h2>

    <p class="muted">
      Signals describe what the system observes. Metrics define how those observations are measured.
    </p>

    <div class="grid2 grid2--equal">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Signals</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Signals are the <strong>inputs</strong> the system monitors across workflows.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Candidate responsiveness</li>
          <li>Pass-through rates</li>
          <li>Decision latency</li>
          <li>Interview loop capacity</li>
          <li>Communication quality</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Metrics</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Metrics define <strong>how signals are measured</strong> and calculated.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Formula</li>
          <li>Grain and filters</li>
          <li>Data fields</li>
          <li>Owner and governance</li>
        </ul>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

